Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:10:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Nothing retires on a STALE reference either, and the 7th
 destructive path was undeclared

TWO L1.37 HOLES, ONE OF THEM LIVE ON THIS BOX RIGHT NOW.

certificate_truth.apply's `lane_settled` gate caught the EMPTY half of the 837-row
incident (n > 0, attestation exact, nothing restorable) and never the STALE half.
Measured here today: the authority was EXACT with 52 rows and 3.2h old against a 2.0h
lease -- settled by every clause it checked, its writer silent since -- with 264
unbacked clocks and 67 ledger claims standing ready to retire on it. A store past its
lease is UNMEASURED, and UNMEASURED is a verdict about the measurement, never about the
world. `require_live_reference` now judges the file the audit ACTUALLY used
(`canon.source`) and its verdict is ANDed into `lane_settled`; the ledger branch, which
was never behind that gate at all, is gated by the same state. A BANNED_CLAIM still
leaves on the decision -- a ban is not a measurement. What is withheld is published as
`skipped.claims_on_unmeasured_canon` and the refusal is appended to
reports/REFERENCE_STANDDOWNS.jsonl, where an operator meets it without asking.

THE SEVENTH UNDECLARED CANDIDATE, which is what was refusing every push:
forward_cure_route.accumulate, shipped this morning, pops rows out of a PERSISTED
roster. Not an in-memory pop, not a false positive -- it has a row now. Declaring it
found a real absence-inference one field down: a validity gate MISSING from a present
verdict read as VALIDITY_FAIL, and 32,773 of the 140,090 verdicts in the live gate
report carry non-empty stages with no validity gate in them at all. A gate now fails
only when its stage is present and says so. Undeclared is back to 6 against a ceiling
of 6; the ceiling did not move.

UNGUARDED_CEILING 2 -> 0. Nothing declared removes on an unproved reference any more, so
the ratchet is now the floor: the next unguarded row fails the gate.

The lint gate was RED IN HEAD for everyone -- 35 I001 import-sort errors in
tests/scripts, landed by an adoption commit -- so ops/gates.sh refused every push from
this box regardless of what was being pushed. Fixed with ruff's own --fix; all four fast
gates are green.

